WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.720
CodeTalk (Rethinking IDE Accessibility)

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.140
Modern IDEs like Visual Studio have taken

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.880
great strides to make their tools usable by visually impaired people.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:16.050
But, they're far from making it an enjoyable experience.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:20.550
Due to the linear nature of information flow between the IDE, screen

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.620
reader and the user, a lot of features

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:28.950
are not accessible to the screen users that the sighted users take for granted.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:32.500
These features can be grouped into three categories:

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.080
Glanceability:

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:38.920
The ability of a sighted developer to quickly glance through tremendous

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.540
amounts of code, structure, and debugging information.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:48.720
This is completely unavailable to a visually impaired user due to screen reader limitations

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:54.420
Debugging information such as break points are also not accessible to visually impaired users.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.460
Navigability:

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:03.500
The ability to quickly navigate through code. Since visually impaired users cannot glance at

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.480
code structure, skipping and moving between functions comments and blocks

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.414
of code, becomes very cumbersome.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.180
Alertability:

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:18.040
Visual Studio gives the developer real-time added information through visual cues.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:21.900
This is completely inaccessible to a screen reader user.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:27.380
CodeTalk is a Visual Studio plugin that aims to address these issues.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:33.220
With CodeTalk, visually impaired developers can quickly navigate through code, get access to real-time

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:37.900
error information, and debug with a completely new debugging experience

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:39.380
we call TalkPoints.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:49.440
For more details visit aka.ms/CodeTalk.

